Where heavy, where bare:
 free <=1.43 : heavy disc out to r~0.125 (a~10.5-12), bare gap 0.125-0.15, one very heavy thin ring 0.15-0.175 (a~45),
               bare/near-bare 0.175-0.25, heavy band 0.25-0.375 (a~10-21), completely bare from r=0.375 to the rim. Cap binds (mass 1.43).
 free <=12   : heavy disc out to r~0.1 (a~110-185), bare 0.1-0.15, one very heavy thin ring 0.15-0.175 (a~360), bare 0.175-0.25,
               heavy band 0.25-0.40 (a~50-130), bare from 0.40 to the rim. Cap binds (mass 12).
 mono <=12   : two piled plateaus: a~75.8 out to r~0.225-0.25, a~52.8 out to r~0.425-0.45, bare beyond 0.45; plus a bump (a~135) in the
               innermost ring r<0.025. Cap binds (mass 12).
Trust:
 - numbers for a given load: good to ~1e-6 in miss (Bessel matching reproduces the bare Bessel zeros to 6 d.p.).
 - free 1.43: 35 of 38 starts land on the same 0.00766 (400-cell); I trust it as the 40-ring optimum to ~1e-5, not proven global.
 - free 12: only 10 of 35 starts reach the best; a ladder of local optima 0.00529..0.00559. Least trusted; could be lower.
 - mono 12: essentially all 125 starts give 0.011979. Trusted as the 40-ring monotone optimum.
 - all three are 40-equal-ring answers: thin spikes one ring wide say the true (free-shape) optimum wants narrower/denser features, so a
   finer or free-edged discretisation should go somewhat lower. I did not test other ring counts in the blind step.

